# Windsurf rules

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repository root before making changes and follow it.

- Milestone-driven development, one milestone at a time
  (`docs/architecture.md` section 29; status in
  `docs/implementation-status.md`).
- Required gates: `make format`, `make lint`, `make unit`, `make coverage`,
  `make build` must all pass from the repository root.
- Non-negotiable integrity rules: only the CLI, orchestrator, and glyph
  catalog may see the requested plaintext; downstream events must never
  contain expected-character fields (`docs/architecture.md` section 7).
- Pin every dependency and container version; no floating `latest` tags.
- Do not combine service languages or bypass required protocols.
- Do not add explanatory comments; write idiomatic, readable code.
- Never commit unless explicitly authorized.
